              <string>2</string>
            </entry>
          </parameters>
        </p>
        <wikiDocumentRevision revision="2">
          <p>
            <parameters>
              <entry>
                <string>revision_author</string>
                <string>XWiki.5be2ea7a421c5f44fc455eec</string>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <string>revision_date</string>
                <date>2023-02-04 09:47:14.639 UTC</date>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <string>title</string>
                <string>How-tos</string>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <string>content</string>
                <string>Explain what this how-to article is for. For example, you might write an article to teach people at your company how to set up a corporate email account or file an expense report.

== {{id name="How-tos-🔵️Instructions"/}}🔵️ Instructions ==

Create a step-by-step guide:

(% start="1" %)
1. Add steps that are simple and self-contained
1. Add illustrations to instructions by typing /image
1. Stick to 3-5 steps per task to avoid overloading readers

{{info}}
Highlight important information in a panel like this one. To edit this panel's color or style, select one of the options in the menu.
{{/info}}

== {{id name="How-tos-🔵️Relatedarticles"/}}🔵️ Related articles ==

The content by label feature automatically displays related articles based on labels you choose. To edit options for this feature, select the placeholder and tap the pencil icon.</string>
