    <wikiSpace name="How to install XWiki">
      <wikiDocument name="WebHome">
        <wikiDocumentLocale>
          <p>
            <parameters>
              <entry>
                <string>creation_author</string>
                <string>XWiki.5be2ea7a421c5f44fc455eec</string>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <string>creation_date</string>
                <date>2023-02-04 09:46:51.23 UTC</date>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <string>lastrevision</string>
                <string>2</string>
              </entry>
            </parameters>
          </p>
          <wikiDocumentRevision revision="2">
            <p>
              <parameters>
                <entry>
                  <string>revision_author</string>
                  <string>XWiki.557058:d542c162-e8ab-47d1-93d0-9ea65b6f28ea</string>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <string>revision_date</string>
                  <date>2026-03-27 10:03:42.809 UTC</date>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <string>title</string>
                  <string>How to install XWiki</string>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <string>content</string>
                  <string>XWiki is a Java-based wiki and runs on a Servlet Container such as Tomcat, Jetty, JBoss, WebLogic, WebSphere, etc. It also uses a relational database to store its content. It can run on almost any database (MySQL, PostgreSQL, etc) but XWiki and the database need to be setup correctly.

See 

{{jira id="System Jira" source="list" style="enum" fields=""}}
KAN-20
{{/jira}}

{{jira id="System Jira" source="list" style="enum" fields=""}}
KAN-20
{{/jira}}

If you're upgrading an existing XWiki install check the [[Upgrade instructions page>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Upgrade||shape="rect"]].

Pick one of the [[installation methods>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Installation/#HInstallationMethods||shape="rect"]] to begin installing XWiki.

Once you've finished the installation check the other topics in the [[Admin Guide>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/||shape="rect"]] for configuring and [[securing>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Security||shape="rect"]] your wiki.

{{toc/}}

= {{id name="HowtoinstallXWiki-HardwareandSoftwarerequirements"/}}Hardware and Software requirements =

* A [[supported Java version>>url:https://dev.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Community/SupportStrategy/JavaSupportStrategy/||shape="rect"]].
* A Servlet Container supporting Servlet 3.1 (Servlet 3.0.1 for XWiki version &lt; 12). Check the [[Servlet Containers officially supported by XWiki devs>>url:https://dev.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Community/ServletContainerSupportStrategy/||shape="rect"]].
* A Database and a JDBC 4.2 Driver for your database (JDBC 4 was required for XWiki versions &lt; 11.5). Check the [[databases offically supported by XWiki devs>>url:https://dev.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Community/DatabaseSupportStrategy||shape="rect"]].
* A supported browser to access XWiki. Check the [[browsers offically supported by XWiki devs>>url:https://dev.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Community/BrowserSupportStrategy||shape="rect"]].
* Enough memory, check the [[Memory section>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Performances/#HMemory||shape="rect"]] of the [[Performance Guide>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Performances/||shape="rect"]].
* Enough [[CPU and RAM>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Performances/#HSizing||shape="rect"]]
* Check the [[release notes>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/ReleaseNotes/||shape="rect"]] for the version you're installing to see what browsers and databases have been tested for it, and to see specific requirements/installation steps. You can also check our [[general support strategy>>url:https://dev.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Community/SupportStrategy||shape="rect"]].
* If you're running XWiki on a server without a display, pass the following Java System Property to the JVM running your Servlet Container: {{code language="none"}}-Djava.awt.headless=true{{/code}}.

{{time datetime="2021-01-21"/}}

= {{id name="HowtoinstallXWiki-InstallationMethods"/}}Installation Methods =

For testing XWiki, we highly recommend one of the following installation method:

* (((
[[Using XWiki in the cloud>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Hosted/||shape="rect"]]

~: This is by far the simplest to try XWiki since you don't need to install anything.
)))
* (((
[[Using a standalone distribution >>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/InstallationStandalone||shape="rect"]]

~: Provides a built-in XWiki, with a portable database (HSQLDB) and a lightweight Java container (Jetty). This standalone distribution is not recommended in a production environment (check the [[DB limitations>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Installation/InstallationWAR/InstallationHSQL/||shape="rect"]]). If you need to use it in a production basis, you may look at the other options.
)))
* (((
[[Using an official XWiki Docker image>>url:https://hub.docker.com/_/xwiki/||shape="rect"]]

~: Provides an easy solution to test XWiki, with a configuration very close to a production setup. You can also use this method in production if you're used to putting Docker images in production.
)))

For production installations, we recommend the following installation method:

* (((
[[Using .deb package (usable for production)>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/InstallationViaAPT||shape="rect"]]

~: Provides a .deb package that can be used on a Debian-based operating system. It can be installed with {{code language="none"}}dpkg{{/code}} or {{code language="none"}}apt{{/code}}; installation is thus automated.
)))

Last, you could manually deploy XWiki as a WAR into the Servlet Container of your choice and on the Database of your choice, if the previous methods were not good enough for your needs. Beware that this requires some technical knowledge about Servlet Container and Databses:

* (((
[[Using .war package (usable for production)>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/InstallationWAR||shape="rect"]]

~: Provides a Java application package that has to be installed in a Java container (such as Tomcat). This can be used on almost any operating system.
)))

Whatever the installation method, you should make sure to [[create the database indexes manually for indexes that are not created automatically>>url:https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Performances/Database%20Administration/||shape="rect"]].

{{confluence-adf-decision-item local-id="db8314ca-8442-4c87-8789-50aefecf4965" state="DECIDED"}}
other installation methods
{{/confluence-adf-decision-item}}

{{confluence-adf-decision-list local-id="a45d5205-98d7-41b7-ab3c-4bafe8294546"/}}

= {{id name="HowtoinstallXWiki-OtherInstallationMethods"/}}Other Installation Methods =

This section is about other, non-official ways of installing XWiki that have been contributed by the community.

Tutorials external to the [[xwiki.org>>url:http://xwiki.org||shape="rect"]] site have not been validated for correctness by the XWiki Development Team and it's also possible that they are out of date or even not working.

* [[How to install XWiki on Debian 9>>url:https://linuxhostsupport.com/blog/how-to-install-xwiki-on-debian-9/||shape="rect"]]
* (((
[[Ansible playbook for installing XWiki>>url:https://github.com/rastandy/xwiki-ansible-playbook||shape="rect"]]

 
)))
* [[Using yaourt on Arch Linux>>url:https://github.com/xwiki-contrib/packaging-archlinux||shape="rect"]]
* [[XWiki On OpenShift (Platform-as-a-Service)>>url:https://github.com/rkmallik/xwiki-example||shape="rect"]]
* (((
[[XWiki On Windows>>url:http://agoncalves.developpez.com/tutoriels/xwiki/creer-un-site-associatif/||shape="rect"]]

 (French)
)))
* (((
